---
import ToolLayout from '../components/ToolLayout.astro';
import ExamTool from '../tools/exam/ExamTool';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Exam photo and signature resizer: exact pixels and KB | iDuckImg"
  description="Resize your photo, signature or thumb impression to the exact pixel size and file size an exam form asks for. Requirements copied from official notices, with sources. Free, in your browser."
  heading="Exam photo and signature resizer"
>
  <ExamTool client:load />
  <section slot="content" class="prose">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Pick your exam and the document you need to upload, or enter your own size.</li>
      <li>Drop your photo or scan. HEIC photos from an iPhone work too.</li>
      <li>Download a JPG that is the right size in pixels and inside the allowed KB range.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      The picture is cut or padded to the exact pixel size, then saved at the best quality that fits under
      the maximum. If a form also asks for a minimum size and a simple picture comes out smaller, harmless
      filler data is added to the JPG file so it reaches the minimum. The picture itself is unchanged by
      that step.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      We list only requirements we have read in official notices, each with a link to the document and
      the date we read it. If your exam is not listed, choose "Other exam" and type the sizes from your
      notice.
    </p>
  </section>
</ToolLayout>
